    "c16": {
      "anchor": "plain-card",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "can we figure out a nice way to make the quotes overlap the bubble?  Maybe with a font with a prettier curly quote",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:00:10.440Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "card",
      "offset": 2,
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:00:38.698Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:00.687Z",
          "html": "<p>Tried five ways, screenshots compared: Georgia's quotes at two sizes, Inter's, Libre Baskerville's, and Playfair Display's bold ones. Playfair's won: rounder, heavier marks. Offline it falls back to Georgia's.</p><p>C25 then moved them inside the pill's white, darker; C29 4px nearer its round ends.</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every quoted pill on both pages; the font is a Google Font loaded by <code>bubbly.css</code>.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:06:33.707Z"
      }
    },
    "c17": {
      "anchor": "plain-to-test-card-setup",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "",
      "excerpt": "",
      "text": "italic?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-11T02:01:26.617Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "\"queen of spades\"",
      "offset": 116,
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:01:27.388Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:02.721Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes: a text in a step is italic, <i>\"queen of spades\"</i>, its quotes too.</p><p>The rule I applied, for C17-C19: in a step, a VALUE is italic (a text, a number, yes and no, a list's value such as <i>queen</i> or <i>spades</i>, and a phrase the project declares, as it's called: <i>is a face card</i>); a REFERENCE is bold (<b>its name</b>, <b>the deck</b>, <b>a new card</b>). On a declaration's own line, a typed value is a pill instead (C26-C28).</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every step on the page.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:07:29.117Z"
      }
    },
    "c18": {
      "anchor": "plain-to-test-card-setup",
      "kind": "section",
