      "at": "2026-11-11T02:01:37.062Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "is a face card",
      "offset": 212,
      "edited": "2026-11-11T02:01:45.710Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-11T02:27:04.850Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes: a phrase the project declares, called in a step, is italic, all its words: <i>is a face card</i>, <i>is a number card</i>, <i>is a queen</i>, <i>is the queen of spades</i>, <i>is not a face card</i>, and the two sided view's <i>is face up</i>. The same everywhere on the page (<code>if it <i>is a club</i></code>, <code>red if it <i>is a diamond</i></code>).</p>\n<epic-net-effect><ul><li>Every phrase call in a step; the rule is in C17's answer.</li></ul></epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-11T02:07:31.451Z"
      }
    },
